  "_comment": "Hand judgement for C2 (content v71). All 455 items were read. C2's floor is 2, so the judgement is 'is this the hard end of C2 or typical C2?'. The hard end is the structure the level is built on — inversion after a negative adverbial, the mixed and unreal conditional, the quantifier-phrase agreement trap — whether the item asks for it in a choice, a blank or out loud; the reading questions that ask what the passage implies or why, rather than a fact it states; and the metalanguage items that name a device where a near-synonym would be wrong. In the other direction, 18 one-clause sentence productions came down to 2: writing 'The isogloss runs just north of the river' after studying it is guided production, not the hard end of the level — the rule B1's and C1's passes set.",
